  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WASH response for South Sudanese population and host communities in White Nile State</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will mainly focus towards filling the gaps and needs in hygiene promotion and public health areas that are currently not being covered by the UNHCR and UNICEF projects which are mainly focusing on Water and Sanitation.  The strategic requirement for this project will be to cater for hygiene needs for the target population through hygiene promotion messaging, and general cleaning campaigns in addition to ongoing latrine rehabilitation and emptying to improve the health and wellbeing of the refugees in Um Sangour camp, Alagaya camp and Dabat Bosin camp. This process is aimed at hygiene behaviour change and will take some time to achieve the desired objectives due to continued influx of refugees into these camps which has increased the hygiene and public health promotion needs. CAFOD hygiene interventions will be focussing on three camps of Alagaya, Dabat Bosin and Um Sangor.  Plan Sudan is implementing hygiene activities in the remaining camps.</narrative>
  </description>
